title: 'statement-store: a changed affinity filter syncs only the newly matched statements'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A peer whose affinity filter changes now receives only the statements that its new filter
    matches and its previous one did not. Before, every filter message restarted a full initial
    sync, so each RPC subscribe or unsubscribe made every peer resend everything the node is a
    DHT target for. A filter repeated unchanged still asks for the full replay, which is how a
    node recovers after major sync, and the first filter after connect still gets the full sync.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
